==About==
To be held in Charlotte, North Carolina, USA {{Flag|us}} The event will be the first international event in 2 years to have a live audience attend.
<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.ubisoft.com/en-au/esports/rainbow-six/siege/news-updates/1RWT8z5Z04MAe03u2PSbJR/introducing-the-six-charlotte-major-from-may-16-to-22|title=INTRODUCING THE SIX CHARLOTTE MAJOR FROM MAY 16 TO 22|publisher=[[Ubisoft]]|date=2022-14-03}}</ref>
On May 9th it was announced that due to visa issues {{TeamIcon|Team oNe eSports}}[[Team oNe eSports|Team oNe]], {{TeamIcon|w7m esports}}[[w7m esports|w7m]], and {{TeamIcon|FURIA Esports}}[[FURIA Esports|FURIA]] would be unable to travel to the United States, and would instead be competing from the Ubisoft Broadcast Studio in Mexico City.
<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/R6esports/status/1523694283705835520|title=An Update on the Six Major Charlotte Teams.|publisher=[[Ubisoft]]|date=2022-05-09}}</ref>
{{TeamIcon|Elevate}}[[Elevate]] would be forced to drop from the event on May 15th, as the team could not obtain their visas to the United States or Mexico. They would be given a placement in the 13-16th place, receive $5,000 {{Abbr/USD}} and 50 [[Six_Invitational/2023/Global_Standings|Global Standings Points]]. <ref>{{cite_web|url=https://twitter.com/R6esports/status/1525521548483993600|title=Competition update on the Six Charlotte Major.|publisher='''[[R6esports]]'''|date=2022-05-15}}</ref><ref>{{cite_web|url=https://twitter.com/ElevateGG/status/1525521321752506370?s=20&t=M0cpItrwAJZeMBBgcjG0zQ|title=Update regarding #ElevateR6 for the Charlotte Major.|publisher='''[[Elevate]]'''|date=2022-05-15}}</ref>

